WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.063
Radiometric thermal sensors record measurement data for pixels or defined areas within stated limits.

00:00:07.063 --> 00:00:10.936
Non-radiometric sensors primarily provide relative visual contrast.

00:00:10.936 --> 00:00:18.910
Both can support observation, but only appropriate radiometric systems should be used for qualified temperature measurement.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:28.252
Resolution affects spatial detail, while thermal sensitivity describes the sensor's ability to distinguish small temperature differences under specified conditions.

00:00:28.252 --> 00:00:31.213
Refresh rate affects motion rendering.

00:00:31.213 --> 00:00:35.998
None of these specifications alone guarantees a useful inspection.

00:00:35.998 --> 00:00:40.783
Sensitivity is not the same as absolute measurement accuracy.

00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:52.402
A sensor may display subtle contrast while the numerical value still depends on calibration, target coverage, emissivity assumptions, reflected radiation, range, and environmental conditions.

00:00:52.402 --> 00:00:57.642
Lens field of view controls scene coverage and target size.

00:00:57.642 --> 00:01:04.705
A wider view covers more area but places fewer pixels on a small target.

00:01:04.705 --> 00:01:11.768
A narrower view can improve target detail from an appropriate distance while reducing context.

00:01:11.768 --> 00:01:16.553
Calibration supports consistency between detector response and reported values.

00:01:16.553 --> 00:01:24.527
Some systems perform internal correction automatically, but calibration status, warm-up, range, and environmental assumptions still matter.

00:01:24.527 --> 00:01:27.489
Follow manufacturer and organizational procedures.

00:01:27.489 --> 00:01:33.640
Drone-mounted payloads add vibration, movement, changing angle, altitude, wind, and flight-safety constraints.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:42.982
The aircraft must carry the payload safely, preserve required clearance, and collect enough stable target pixels for the mission.

00:01:42.982 --> 00:01:45.944
Match capability to the question.

00:01:45.944 --> 00:01:58.019
Screening for broad anomalies, measuring a small electrical connection, mapping a roof, and supporting fire awareness have different sensor, lens, distance, timing, and expertise requirements.

00:01:58.019 --> 00:02:01.436
Define acceptable uncertainty before selecting equipment.
